.TH D7-MIGRATE 1 "17 September 2026" "Andromeda" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
d7-migrate \- Drupal 7 / BOA to Backdrop on a Andromeda host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B andromeda
.RB [ \-n ]
.B d7
.I verb
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B d7-migrate
.RB [ \-n ]
.I verb
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Convert a Drupal 7 site (often live on a BOA / Aegir VPS) into a
Backdrop product on knarr.
.PP
This is
.I not
a Drupal 8+ Migrate API pipeline.
Backdrop is a Drupal 7 fork.
The conversion is: import the D7 dump into an empty database, put
ported modules on disk, then
.B bee \-y update-db
(same path as
.BR core/update.php ).
Never run
.B bee install
on that database.
.PP
On knarr,
.B d7-migrate
execs
.B andromeda d7
when Andromeda is installed and you are not root.
On a BOA box it sources
.B lib/d7.sh
directly.
.SH VERBS
.TP
.B test SITE
Scan modules, themes, settings, and inventory.
Writes
.BR plan.json ,
.BR playbook.txt ,
.BR modules.tsv ,
.BR steps.tsv ,
.BR status.tsv ,
.B TUTORIAL.txt
under
.BR \-\-out .
Ubercart / Rules / Search API steps only if those modules are enabled.
.TP
.B apply \-\-plan DIR
Run automatable steps from the plan.
.B \-\-step ID
runs one.
.B \-\-yes
skips prompts.
.B \-n
prints commands.
.TP
.B tutorial \-\-plan DIR
Reprint the leftover-work tutorial for that site.
.TP
.B prep \-\-from SITE
Snapshot SQL (gzip), public/private files, site modules/themes,
and BOA
.B sites/all/modules/{custom,features}
plus themes and libraries.
.TP
.B assess \-\-from SITE|BUNDLE
Classify enabled projects against
.BR lib/d7-catalog.txt .
Exits 1 if an enabled project has no Backdrop port unless
.B \-\-force .
.TP
.B convert \-\-from BUNDLE \-\-platform NAME \-\-product NAME
Create utf8mb4 DB, import dump, truncate
.BR cache_* ,
copy files and custom code, patch theme
.B .info
files, download ports, run
.B bee \-y update-db ,
cache-rebuild.
.TP
.B attach \-\-platform NAME \-\-product NAME
Apache alias and
.B andromeda site-check .
.TP
.B toolkit PLATFORM
Download
.BR coder_upgrade ,
.BR default_views_config ,
.BR entity_plus ,
.BR entity_ui ,
.B d7compatible
(and
.B rules_cmi
only if Rules was scanned).
.TP
.B stubs
Write empty D7 stub modules the scan said you need
.RB ( entity_plus
/
.B entity_ui
and
.B ubercart
only when
.B uc_*
is enabled).
.TP
.B theme-patch \-\-platform NAME \-\-product NAME
Set
.B backdrop = 1.x
and
.B base theme = d7compatible
on copied D7 themes.
.TP
.B cex \-\-platform NAME \-\-product NAME
.B bee config-export
(active JSON to staging).
.TP
.B port \-\-from MODULE_DIR \-\-platform NAME
Wrap
.B coder_upgrade
for one custom module.
.TP
.B tools
Print the official Backdrop testers and what Andromeda wraps.
.TP
.B all
prep + assess + convert + attach.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Dry-run.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Answer safe prompts yes (write stubs, run auto apply steps).
.TP
.B \-\-from DIR
Site directory or prep bundle.
.TP
.B \-\-out DIR
Bundle / plan directory.
.TP
.B \-\-plan DIR
Plan directory (or path to
.BR plan.json ).
.TP
.B \-\-step ID
Single apply step.
.TP
.B \-\-platform NAME
.TQ
.B \-\-product NAME
.TQ
.B \-\-host HOST
.TP
.B \-\-alias @site
Drush alias on the BOA box.
.TP
.B \-\-sql FILE
.TQ
.B \-\-files DIR
.TQ
.B \-\-private DIR
.TP
.B \-\-force
Assess does not fail on missing ports.
.TP
.B \-\-skip-dl
Convert does not
.B bee download
ports.
.TP
.B \-\-keep-update-access
Leave
.B $update_free_access = TRUE
after convert.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B lib/d7.sh
Module sourced by
.B andromeda
and
.BR d7-migrate .
.TP
.B lib/d7-catalog.txt
COREIN / DROP / REPLACE / CONTRIB / STUB map.
.TP
.B docs/d7-migration.txt
New-sysadmin handbook.
.TP
.B DIR/plan.json
Machine plan written by
.BR test .
.TP
.B DIR/TUTORIAL.txt
Leftover human steps after
.BR apply .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR andromeda (1),
.BR crdir (1),
docs/d7-migration.txt,
https://docs.backdropcms.org/documentation/upgrading-from-drupal-7-overview
.SH NOTES
Do not prefix
.B andromeda
with
.BR sudo .
Operator user only.
.PP
JSON config for settings, Views stored in
.BR {views_view} ,
and most variables is written by each module's
.B hook_update_N
during
.BR update-db .
.B bee config-export
is how that JSON moves between devel / test / live.
Code-only default Views still need
.BR default_views_config .
